   "source": [
    "# Zetaris connection test\n",
    "\n",
    "Try the Zetaris cluster from Python **before** we change the app. Run the cells top to bottom.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Settings**: where the cluster is and how to log in (read from `.env`, never typed into the notebook).\n",
    "2. **Can we reach it?** A simple check of the addresses.\n",
    "3. **Find the API**: which web addresses Zetaris uses for login and SQL.\n",
    "4. **Log in** and **run a query**: `SELECT * FROM NY_TAXI.taxi_zones LIMIT 5` should give 5 rows.\n",
    "5. **Our data**: the same query through Zetaris and on the local files should match.\n",
    "\n",
    "When step 4 works, send the endpoint names and one response shape (no passwords or tokens) and the app adapter (`app/adapters/zetaris.py`) gets updated to match."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Settings\n",
    "\n",
    "Add these lines to `bus-buddy-upload/.env` (the file is never committed):\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "ZETARIS_SIGNIN_URL=<Sign-in URL from the cluster's Overview > Access page>\n",
    "ZETARIS_REST_URL=<REST / API address, if Overview > Access shows one>\n",
    "ZETARIS_EMAIL=<admin email from Organisations>\n",
    "ZETARIS_PASSWORD=<admin password from Organisations>\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "If the password is not in `.env`, the next cell asks for it without showing it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import getpass, json, os, socket, sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from urllib.parse import urljoin, urlparse\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "\n",
    "try:   # use the computer's own trusted certificates (fixes CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED on many Windows setups)\n",
    "    import truststore\n",
    "    truststore.inject_into_ssl()\n",
    "    print(\"certificates   : using this computer's trusted certificates (truststore)\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    print(\"certificates   : truststore NOT installed for this kernel:\", sys.executable)\n",
    "    print(\"                 install it, then RESTART the kernel and run this cell again\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == \"notebooks\" else Path.cwd()\n",
    "load_dotenv(ROOT / \".env\")\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "def setting(name):\n",
    "    v = os.getenv(name, \"\").strip()\n",
    "    return \"\" if v.startswith(\"<\") else v     # ignore a leftover <placeholder>\n",
    "\n",
    "SIGNIN_URL = setting(\"ZETARIS_SIGNIN_URL\")\n",
    "_u = urlparse(setting(\"ZETARIS_REST_URL\") or SIGNIN_URL)\n",
    "API_BASE = f\"{_u.scheme}://{_u.netloc}\" if _u.netloc else \"\"   # site address only; API paths start with /api/...\n",
    "EMAIL = setting(\"ZETARIS_EMAIL\")\n",
    "PASSWORD = os.getenv(\"ZETARIS_PASSWORD\") or getpass.getpass(\"Zetaris password: \")\n",
    "ORG_ID = setting(\"ZETARIS_ORG_ID\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def hide(text, secrets=(PASSWORD,)):\n",
    "    # never print a password or token by accident\n",
    "    text = str(text)\n",
    "    for s in secrets:\n",
    "        if s and len(s) > 3:\n",
    "            text = text.replace(s, \"***\")\n",
    "    return text\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"project folder :\", ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"sign-in URL    :\", SIGNIN_URL or \"(missing: add ZETARIS_SIGNIN_URL to .env)\")\n",
    "print(\"API base       :\", API_BASE or \"(missing)\")\n",
    "print(\"email set      :\", bool(EMAIL))\n",
    "print(\"password set   :\", bool(PASSWORD))"
   ]
  },
